/// c_prototype.hu - The shape of a C function prototype.
///
/// This is the form framework/c_compiler.bsh deals in when it compiles a
/// native library at runtime, which is why it is the worked example: the
/// description is of syntax this project already emits and reads.

$root IS "CPrototype"
$root CAN HAVE ONE OR MORE $prototype

A $prototype ENDS WITH ';'
A $prototype HAS:
1. The $returnType, that IS a #word
2. The $name of the function, that IS an #identifier
3. The $parameters that ARE INSIDE '(', ')'

$parameters CAN HAVE ONE OR MORE $parameter SEPARATED BY ','
A $parameter HAS:
1. The $type, that IS a #word
2. The $argument, that IS an #identifier
